WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.033
Hello, I'm Gav.

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.866
I'm Dan.

00:00:01.866 --> 00:00:02.699
We're The Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:04.380
Yeah, back in 'Bama with this beast again.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.550
This is our new favorite beast.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.180
We just had to use it for another video.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.800
In this video, we're gonna simulate

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.060
what it might be like
to get sniped in the eye

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.430
with a .50 cal sniper rifle.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.540
Just so you don't have to.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.170
Just so you don't have to
go through that yourself.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.289
We're gonna use the V2511

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:20.090
and a mirror placed at 45 degrees.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.853
So we don't actually have to
shoot the Phantom in the face.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.330
Full sun, you good?

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:38.693
All right, Dan, give me
your best and only shot.

00:00:52.161 --> 00:00:52.994
I think we're good.

00:00:52.994 --> 00:00:54.090
Well, you broke the mirror.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.370
Yeah.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.203
Wow.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.040
Goodness, one second the mirror was there.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.313
I looked again and it was just gone.

00:01:21.375 --> 00:01:23.335
Were you nervous at this point?

00:01:23.335 --> 00:01:24.820
I just wanted to get a
shot right, you know,

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.720
didn't wanna miss.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.570
Ooh.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.950
Can you see the bullet?
It's coming straight--

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.160
That is the bullet.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.110
That dot in front of
the smoke is the bullet.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:38.943
Wow, so--

00:01:38.943 --> 00:01:40.140
It's just is gonna get bigger

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.160
and more soft until it hits the lens.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.960
That is terrifying,
I've never seen a bullet

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.910
just not move in any direction
apart from towards it.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:48.743
Yeah.

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:11.533
Ooh, right in the middle there, jeez.

00:02:13.306 --> 00:02:14.223
Goodness.

00:02:15.826 --> 00:02:17.590
Wow.
That was a damn good shot.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.444
That's the light at the end
of the tunnel right there.

00:02:20.444 --> 00:02:25.444
God, you think you'd hear
the shot that killed ya.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.465
No you wouldn't.
Probably not.

00:02:26.465 --> 00:02:27.863
You wouldn't know anything about it.

00:02:34.443 --> 00:02:36.310
It just looks like it disappeared.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:37.920
That's so weird, I guess,

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.940
because I was focused through the mirror,

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.880
but you were the same distance
away as that burn behind it.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.190
You can't see the edge of the mirror.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.080
It just blurs off.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.500
Oh, oh right, so wait.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.952
So they're both in focus?

00:02:47.952 --> 00:02:48.785
What's in the distance

00:02:48.785 --> 00:02:49.618
and me.
You were in focus

00:02:49.618 --> 00:02:50.910
and what's behind the mirror's in focus.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.770
When I first saw it, I didn't even realize

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.860
that the edges of the mirror were there.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.693
Yeah, completely, look.
And then it's hard to tell

00:02:55.693 --> 00:02:57.180
that the mirror actually
didn't fill the frame

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.540
but the blur made it look like it did.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.730
It looks like in some
sort of weird valley.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.345
What an unexpected side effect.

00:03:04.345 --> 00:03:05.960
And it's an amazing shot

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.370
And also it was an amazing shot.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.370
Ah thanks, yes, good job and good job.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:11.303
Well done, well done.

00:03:11.303 --> 00:03:12.136
Thank you, sir.

00:03:12.136 --> 00:03:14.860
Well Dan, that was absolutely
terrifying high speed,

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.693
I thought.

00:03:15.693 --> 00:03:16.526
So scary,

00:03:16.526 --> 00:03:17.530
imagine that.
If I've learned anything

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.550
from this video, it's don't get sniped

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.480
by a .50 cal sniper rifle.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.930
Did you need to learn that?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:23.840
I feel like I already knew it,

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.480
but now I definitely, it's
like a hundred percent

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.670
at this point.
Yeah.

